{"G1138":{"id":"G1138","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1138","disambiguated_id":"G1138 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H1732","headword":"Δαυείδ, Δαυίδ, Δαβίδ","transliteration":"Daueid, Dauid, Dabid","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"David","definition_en":"Δαυείδ (Rec. Δαβίδ), ὁ, indecl. (Heb. דָּוִד), \n David, King of Israel: Mat.1:6; 12:3, and al.; σκηνὴ Δ., Act.15:16; κλεὶς Δ., Rev.3:7; θρόνος Δ., Luk.1:32; ῥίζα Δ., Rev.5:5; βασιλεία Δ., Mrk.11:10; υἱὸς Δ., the Messiah (Ps. Sol., 17:23; for other reff. in Jewish lit., see Dalman, Words, 317), Mat.1:1 9:27, and al.; ἐν Δ., i.e. the Psalter, Heb.4:7 \n (AS)","source_line":1270}],"occurrence_count":59,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Davi","count":59}]},"G1162":{"id":"G1162","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1162","disambiguated_id":"G1162 =","unique_id":"G1162","headword":"δέησις","transliteration":"deēsis","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"petition","definition_en":"δέησις, -εως, ἡ\n (δέομαι), [in LXX for תְּחִנָּה, רִנָּה, תְּפִלָּה, etc. ;] \n __1. a wanting, need (so Ps 21(22):25). \n __2. an asking, entreaty, supplica­tion; in NT always addressed to God: Luk.1:13, 2Co.1:11, Php.1:19, 2Ti.1:3, Jas.5:16, 1Pe.3:12\" (LXX) ; with νηστεῖαι, Luk.2:37; προσυνχή, -αί, Eph.6:18, Php.4:6, 1Ti.2:1 5:5; ἱκετηρίαι, Heb.5:7; προσκαρτέρησις, Eph.6:18; ἐντεύξεις, 1Ti.2:1; δ. ποιεῖσθαι (Deiss., BS, 250), Luk.5:33, Php.1:4 (pl.), 1Ti.2:1; before ὑπέρ, 2Co.9:14, Php.1:4; περί, Eph.6:18; πρός, Rom.10:1.†\n SYN.: προσευχή, used of prayer in general, while δ. gives prominence to the sense of need; on the other hand, δ. is used as well of requests from man to man, while π. is limited to prayer to God. ἔντευξις, in the π., is the regular word for petition to a superior (Deiss., BS, 250; cf. the Pauline ἐντυγχάνειν, to entreat). Cf. also εὐχή. (Jas.5:15), αἴτημα, ἱκετηρία (Tr., Syn., § li; Cremer, 73, 174, 684). (AS)","source_line":1294}],"occurrence_count":18,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"oração","count":7},{"gloss":"orações","count":6},{"gloss":"súplica","count":2},{"gloss":"súplicas-ações","count":1},{"gloss":"pedidos","count":1},{"gloss":"rogos","count":1}]},"G1468":{"id":"G1468","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1468","disambiguated_id":"G1468 =","unique_id":"G1468","headword":"ἐγκρατής","transliteration":"egkratēs","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"self-controlled","definition_en":"ἐγκρατής, -ές \n (κράτος), [in LXX: Wis.8:20, Sir.6:27 15:1 26:15 27:30, al. ;] \n __1. strong, powerful. \n __2. C. genitive of thing(s), master of, hence, \n __3. (sc. ἑαυτοῦ), self -controlled, exercising self-control: Tit.1:8.\n† SYN.: σώφρων (see reff. s. ἐγκράτεια). (AS)","source_line":1600}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"domínio-próprio","count":1}]},"G1877":{"id":"G1877","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1877","disambiguated_id":"G1877 =","unique_id":"G1877","headword":"ἐπανάγω","transliteration":"epanagō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to set off","definition_en":"ἐπ-αν-άγω \n [in LXX: Zec.4:12 (רוּק hi.), Sir.17:26 26:28, 2Ma.9:21 2Mac 12:4 * ;] \nto bring up or back (sc. ναῦς); to put out to sea (DB, iii, 63b): Luk.5:3-4; intrans., to return: Mat.21:18.†\n (AS)","source_line":2018}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"voltava","count":1},{"gloss":"afastasse","count":1},{"gloss":"leva-para","count":1}]},"G2291":{"id":"G2291","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2291","disambiguated_id":"G2291 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H8646G","headword":"Θάρα","transliteration":"Thara","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Terah","definition_en":"Θαρά (Rec. Θάρα), ὁ, indecl. (Heb. תֶּרַח), \n Terah (Gen.11:24-28, 31-32): Luk.3:34.†\n (AS)","source_line":2440}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Terá","count":1}]},"G2862":{"id":"G2862","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2862","disambiguated_id":"G2862 = a Name of","unique_id":"G4514","headword":"κολωνία","transliteration":"kolōnia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"Roman colony","definition_en":"κολωνία (Rec. -ώνια), -ας, ἡ \n (Lat. colonic), \na colony: Act.16:12 (see Lft., Phi., 50 f.).†\n (AS)","source_line":3057}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"colônia","count":1}]},"G2938":{"id":"G2938","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2938","disambiguated_id":"G2938 =","unique_id":"G2938","headword":"κτίσμα","transliteration":"ktisma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"creature","definition_en":"κτίσμα, -τος, τό\n (κτίζω), [in LXX: Wis.9:2 13:5 14:11, Sir.36:20 (17), Sir.38:34, 3Ma.5:11 * ;] \n__1. (cl.) a colony. \n __2. a created thing, creature: 1Ti.4:4, Jas.1:18, Rev.5:13 8:9.†\n (AS)","source_line":3133}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"criatura","count":2},{"gloss":"criaturas","count":2}]},"G294":{"id":"G294","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0294","disambiguated_id":"G0294 =","unique_id":"G0294","headword":"ἀμφιέννυμι","transliteration":"amphiennumi","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to clothe","definition_en":"ἀμφιέννυμι\n (ἕννυμι, to clothe), \nto clothe: Mat.6:30 11:8, Luk.7:25 (cf. ἀμφιάζω).†\n (AS)","source_line":397}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"delicadas","count":2},{"gloss":"veste","count":1}]},"G341":{"id":"G341","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0341","disambiguated_id":"G0341 =","unique_id":"G0341","headword":"ἀνακαινόω","transliteration":"anakainoō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to renew","definition_en":"ἀνα-καινόω, -ῶ\n = ἀνακαινίζω (cf. MM, VGT, see word), \n to make new: 2Co.4:16, Col.3:10 (see Cremer, 323).†\n (AS)","source_line":445}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"se-renova","count":1},{"gloss":"renova","count":1}]},"G3462":{"id":"G3462","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3462","disambiguated_id":"G3462 =","unique_id":"G3462","headword":"μυρίζω","transliteration":"murizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to anoint","definition_en":"μυρίζω\n (μύρον), \nIonic and poët. (comic), \n to anoint: Mrk.14:8.†\n SYN.: see: ἀλείφω, and cf. μύρον (AS)","source_line":3575}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"adiantou","count":1}]},"G3581":{"id":"G3581","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3581","disambiguated_id":"G3581 =","unique_id":"G3581","headword":"ξένος","transliteration":"xenos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"foreign","definition_en":"ξένος, -η, -ον \n [in LXX chiefly for נׇכְרִי ;] \n__(a) foreign, alien: δαιμόνια, Act.17:18; διδαχαί Heb.13:9; \n __(b) with genitive of thing(s), strange to, estranged from, ignorant of: Eph.2:12; \n __(with) strange, unusual: 1Pe.4:12. \n As subst., ὁ ξ., \n __(a) a foreigner, stranger: Mat.25:35, 38 25:43-44 27:7, Act.17:21, 3Jn.5; ξέίνοι κ. τάροικοι (opposite to συμπολῖται, οίκεῖοι), Eph.2:19; ξ. καὶ παρεπίδημοι, Heb.11:13; \n __(b) one of the parties bound by ties of hospitality; \n __α the guest; \n __β the host (= ξενοδόκος, Hom., Ii, xv, 532) : Rom.16:23.†\n (AS)","source_line":3695}],"occurrence_count":14,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"forasteiro","count":4},{"gloss":"estrangeiros","count":4},{"gloss":"de-estranhos","count":1},{"gloss":"hospedeiro","count":1},{"gloss":"estranhos","count":1},{"gloss":"estranhas","count":1},{"gloss":"estranho","count":1},{"gloss":"forasteiros","count":1}]},"G3725":{"id":"G3725","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3725","disambiguated_id":"G3725 =","unique_id":"G3725","headword":"ὅριον","transliteration":"horion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"region","definition_en":"ὅριον, -ου, τό\n (ὅρος, a boundary), [in LXX chiefly for גְּבוּל ;] \na boundary, bound; chiefly in pl., and so always in NT: Mat.2:16 4:13 8:34 15:22, 39 19:1, Mrk.5:17 7:24, 31 10:1, Act.13:50.†\n (AS)","source_line":3842}],"occurrence_count":12,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"região","count":5},{"gloss":"limites","count":4},{"gloss":"território","count":2},{"gloss":"territórios","count":1}]},"G3970":{"id":"G3970","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3970","disambiguated_id":"G3970 =","unique_id":"G3970","headword":"πατροπαράδοτος","transliteration":"patroparadotos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"from forefathers","definition_en":"πατρο-παρά-δοτος, -ον\n (πατήρ, παραδίδωμι), \nhanded down from one's fathers, inherited: 1Pe.1:18 (Diod., al.).†\n (AS)","source_line":4088}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"pais","count":1}]},"G4033":{"id":"G4033","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4033","disambiguated_id":"G4033 =","unique_id":"G4033","headword":"περικυκλόω","transliteration":"perikukloō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to surround","definition_en":"περι-κυκλόω, -ῶ \n [in LXX chiefly for סָבַב ;] \nto encircle, encompass: of a besieged city, Luk.19:43.†\n (AS)","source_line":4155}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"cercarão","count":1}]},"G4055":{"id":"G4055","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4055","disambiguated_id":"G4055 =","unique_id":"G4055","headword":"περισσότερος","transliteration":"perissoteros","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"more excessive","definition_en":"more superabundant rabundant, excess, far fetched, superfluous (in number, degree or character)","source_line":4177}],"occurrence_count":15,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"mais","count":7},{"gloss":"mais-grave","count":2},{"gloss":"muito-mais","count":2},{"gloss":"maior","count":2},{"gloss":"mais-que","count":1},{"gloss":"excessiva","count":1}]},"G4318":{"id":"G4318","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4318","disambiguated_id":"G4318 =","unique_id":"G4318","headword":"προσαγωγή","transliteration":"prosagōgē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"access","definition_en":"προσ-αγωγή, -ῆς, ἡ \n (προσάγω), \n__1. a bringing to. \n __2. approach, access (see Lft., Notes, 284; MM, xxi): Rom.5:2, Eph.2:18 3:12 (but see Ellic., Eph., 59 f., where the transitive sense \"introduction \" is advocated).†\n (AS)","source_line":4448}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"acesso","count":3}]},"G4600":{"id":"G4600","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4600","disambiguated_id":"G4600 =","unique_id":"G4600","headword":"σιαγών","transliteration":"siagōn","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"cheek","definition_en":"σιαγών, -όνος, ἡ \n [in LXX for לְחִי ;] \nthe jawbone, jaw, cheek: Mat.5:39, Luk.6:29 (cf. MM, xxii).†\n (AS)","source_line":4738}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"face","count":2}]},"G4766":{"id":"G4766","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4766","disambiguated_id":"G4766 =","unique_id":"G4766","headword":"στρώννυμι","transliteration":"strōnnumi","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to spread","definition_en":"στρωννύω or στρώννυμι\n (seeBl., § 23, 1; Veitch, see word), [in LXX for יַצַע hoph., etc. ;] \nto spread: ἱμάτια ἐν τ. ὁδῷ (εἰς τ. ὁδόν), Mat.21:8, Mrk.11:8; of making a bed, στρῶσον (sc. τ. κλίνην) σεαυτῷ, Act.9:34; of furnishing a room, ἐστρωμένον, spread with carpets or carpeted couches (cf. Eze.23:41), Mrk.14:15, Luk.22:12.†\n (AS)","source_line":4914}],"occurrence_count":6,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"salão","count":2},{"gloss":"estendia","count":1},{"gloss":"espalhavam","count":1},{"gloss":"estenderam","count":1},{"gloss":"faz-tua","count":1}]},"G5298":{"id":"G5298","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5298","disambiguated_id":"G5298 =","unique_id":"G5298","headword":"ὑποχωρέω","transliteration":"hupochōreō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to withdraw","definition_en":"ὑπο-χωρέω \n [in LXX: Jdg.20:37 B (-), Sir.13:9, 2Ma.12:12 * ;] \nto go back, retire: before ἐν, Luk.5:16; before εἰς, Luk.9:10.†\n (AS)","source_line":5454}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"retirava","count":1},{"gloss":"retirou","count":1}]},"G5487":{"id":"G5487","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5487","disambiguated_id":"G5487 =","unique_id":"G5487","headword":"χαριτόω","transliteration":"charitoō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to favor","definition_en":"χαριτόω, -ῶ\n (χάρις), [in LXX: Sir.18:17 (ἀνδρί κεχαριτωμένῳ; Vg., justificato; Syr., saintly) * ;] \nto endow with χάρις (which see), i.e. \n __1. (a) to make graceful; \n __(b) to make gracious (Sir, l.with). \n __2. In Hellenistic writings (for exx., see AR, Eph., 227; Lft., Notes, 315), \n __(a) to cause to find favour; \n __(b) to endue with grace (i.e. divine favour): Luk.1:28, Eph.1:6.†\n (AS)","source_line":5653}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"agraciada","count":1},{"gloss":"concedeu","count":1}]},"G581":{"id":"G581","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0581","disambiguated_id":"G0581 =","unique_id":"G0581","headword":"ἀπογενόμενος","transliteration":"apogenomenos","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to cease to be","definition_en":"ἀπο-γίνομαι (cl. -γίγν-)\n [in LXX: Da TH Dan.2:1 * ;] \n__1. to be away, removed from. \n __2. to depart life, to die (MM, see word): τ. ἀμαρτίαις, i.e. with ref. to sins, 1Pe.2:24 (Cremer, 149, 668).†\n (AS)","source_line":689}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"vivamos","count":1}]},"G789":{"id":"G789","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0789","disambiguated_id":"G0789 =","unique_id":"G0789","headword":"Ἄσσος","transliteration":"Assos","lexical_morphology":"N:N-F-L","gloss_en":"Assos","definition_en":"Ἄσσος, -ου\n (also Ἀσσός, -οῦ), ή \nAssos, a city on the E. coast of Asia Minor: Act.20:13-14 (see: ἆσσον).†\n (AS)","source_line":901}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Assôs","count":2}]},"G835":{"id":"G835","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0835","disambiguated_id":"G0835 =","unique_id":"G0835","headword":"αὐλίζομαι","transliteration":"aulizomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V",